body:
`notifyRegulators` and `regulatorDeadlineHours` are logically dependent, but the schema currently allows `notifyRegulators: true` without a deadline (and allows a deadline when `notifyRegulators` is false). Consider adding an object-level refinement so `regulatorDeadlineHours` is required (and positive) when `notifyRegulators` is true.
```suggestion
    .describe('Regulatory notification deadline in hours'),
}).superRefine((value, ctx) => {
  if (value.notifyRegulators) {
    if (value.regulatorDeadlineHours == null) {
      ctx.addIssue({
        code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,
        path: ['regulatorDeadlineHours'],
        message: 'regulatorDeadlineHours is required when notifyRegulators is true',
      });
    } else if (value.regulatorDeadlineHours <= 0) {
      ctx.addIssue({
        code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,
        path: ['regulatorDeadlineHours'],
        message: 'regulatorDeadlineHours must be a positive number when notifyRegulators is true',
      });
    }
  } else if (value.regulatorDeadlineHours != null) {
    ctx.addIssue({
      code: z.ZodIssueCode.custom,
      path: ['regulatorDeadlineHours'],
      message: 'regulatorDeadlineHours must be omitted when notifyRegulators is false',
    });
  }
```
